,"kind":"tool_call","text":"src/views/views.ts","tool":"Edit","callId":"call-62"},{"at":"2026-10-06T07:23:00.000Z","kind":"tool_result","text":"周报草稿写好了，放在 docs/weekly/2026-W45.md：本周发了 3 个 beta、1 个正式版，一次事故（relay 证书过期 22 分钟），下周重点是 iOS 上架。","tool":"Edit","ok":true,"callId":"call-62"},{"at":"2026-10-06T07:24:00.000Z","kind":"user","text":"<message via=\"web\" connect=\"ember\" thread=\"EMBER/1001.0\" from=\"左子健 (me@x.com)\" ts=\"1001.000164\">\nHere's what I found in the station worker's memory growth:\n\n- RSS grows ~38 MB/hour with 6 chats open, and never comes back down;\n- heap snapshots at 0 h, 2 h and 6 h show `MdCache` holding 41k entries at the end, 93% of them for archived chats;\n- nothing evicts them: `forget()` is only called when a chat is deleted, never when it is archived.\n\nThe fix (PR #5251):\n\n```ts\nconst cache = new Lru<string, Md>(500, (key) => kept.delete(key));\ndata.onArchived((station, key) => cache.dropWhere((k) => k.startsWith(`${station}\\u0001${key}`)));\n```\n\nAfter it, RSS is flat at 212 MB over 6 hours with the same load. I also added a test that archives 1,000 chats and checks the cache stays at 500.\n\nOne question: should the cap be per workspace or for the whole device? Per device is simpler, but a big workspace could push a small one's chats out.\n</message>"},{"at":"2026-10-06T07:25:00.000Z","kind":"thinking","text":"PR 已经开了：https://github.com/acme/app/pull/5244 ，CI 在跑，大概 12 分钟。"},{"at":"2026-10-06T07:26:00.000Z","kind":"tool_call","text":"pnpm exec tsgo --noEmit && node --test test/views.test.ts","tool":"Read","callId":"call-66"},{"at":"2026-10-06T07:27:00.000Z","kind":"tool_result","text":"✔ 311 tests passed (14.2s)","tool":"Read","ok":true,"callId":"call-66"},{"at":"2026-10-06T07:28:00.000Z","kind":"user","text":"<message via=\"web\" connect=\"ember\" thread=\"EMBER/1001.0\" from=\"Lina Park (lina@acme.dev)\" ts=\"1001.000168\">\n这里的 timeout 我改成了按 Clock 的 sleep，测试里用 TestClock 推进，不再有真实等待。顺便删掉了两个只为了等时间的 retry。\n</message>"},{"at